  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "TossIt",
    "description": "This project is a cross platform (Android and iOS) application that crowd sources waste removal similar to how Uber crowdsources drivers.  The project is to connect those needing to remove or recycle waste and willing to pay a fee to those that are willing to remove it for the fee.  This application is designed using Facebooks's React-Native as the front-end and Google's Firebase as the backend.  It is still an ongoing project that will hopefully be released to Google Play and the Apple Appstore in the near future.\n\nIt is going to feature very quick interactions with Google Maps so people can look for nearby waste they can move extremely easily and post waste that is needed to be removed quickly.  The UX element of the application will be tested to be of industry best practices and through user tests to ensure a complete experience.\n\nThis application will follow the SDLC and hopefully gain traction in the market and become a mini startup.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Jan 2017 - May 2017"
   },
   {
    "title": "Memory Visualizer for the CS220 course at GaTech",
    "description": "It was a year long Junior/Senior Design project using Agile Development principles to develop a visualizer application that can be used in the classroom to help students.  It's aim was to help students learn and understand about memory and cache systems that are taught in the CS2200 course.  The course usually uses hand drawings on a whiteboard to show how each system works and what happens when you have different replacement policies, block sizes, and etc.  This project was to simulate that process dynamically with descriptions that will help the student learn and cut back on the time professors use drawing the systems.  This project is open source and can be used by professors, teaching assistants and students.",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Jan 2016 - Dec 2016"
   }
